\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Behold us, Lord, a little space
\par From daily tasks set free;
\par And met within Thy holy place
\par To rest awhile with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Around us rolls the ceaseless tide 
\par Of business, toil, and care,
\par And scarcely can we turn aside
\par For one brief hour of prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Yet these are not the only walls
\par Wherein Thou may'st be sought;
\par On homeliest work Thy blessing falls 
\par In truth and patience wrought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thine is the loom, the forge, the mart,
\par The wealth of land and sea,
\par The worlds of science and of art,
\par Revealed and ruled by Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then let us prove our heavenly birth
\par In all we do and know,
\par And claim the kingdom of the earth
\par For Thee, and not Thy foe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Work shall be prayer, if all be wrought
\par As Thou wouldst have it done;
\par And prayer, by Thee inspired and taught;
\par Itself with work be one.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

